vpnbox — bundled components and licenses
========================================

vpnbox's own source code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). The released Android
build statically bundles the following components, which keep their original
licenses. The full source of every component is in this repository:

  Component  License                              Source in this repo
  ---------  -----------------------------------  --------------------------------
  OpenVPN 3  AGPL-3.0-only OR MPL-2.0, with the   android/engine/src/main/cpp/
  core       openvpn3-exceptions (OpenSSL link    openvpn3  (submodule, pinned;
             exception; see openvpn3/LICENSE.md)  LICENSES/ holds all texts)
             — this build relies on the MPL-2.0
             alternative for the core sources,
             and the OpenSSL link exception for
             the bundled OpenSSL
  OpenSSL    Apache-2.0 (module marked            android/engine/src/main/cpp/
             BSD_like for Android; NOTICE file    openssl  (submodule, pinned;
             inside)                              NOTICE + LICENSE inside)
  asio       Boost Software License 1.0           android/engine/src/main/cpp/asio
                                                  (submodule; COPYING)
  fmt        MIT                                  android/engine/src/main/cpp/fmt
                                                  (submodule; LICENSE)
  lz4        BSD-2-Clause (command-line parts     android/engine/src/main/cpp/lz4
             GPL-2.0, not used by the app)        (submodule; LICENSE + lib/LICENSE)
  LZO 2.10   GPL-2.0-or-later                     android/engine/src/main/cpp/lzo
             (vendored; COPYING inside)           (vendored; COPYING)

The SWIG-generated JNI bindings under
android/engine/src/main/java/net/openvpn/ovpn3 and the wrapper
android/engine/src/main/cpp/ovpncli_wrap.* were generated from the OpenVPN 3
core headers and carry its license terms.

The complete Android application (vpnbox code + the bundled core above) is
therefore distributed under the compatible set of the licenses above: in
practice the copyleft terms of the strongest component govern redistribution
of the binary, and the corresponding sources for all components are provided
here for every release tag.
